In JavaScript, you can implement bruteforcing by writing a script that generates and tests all possible combinations of characters for a password or solution. Here's a simple example of bruteforcing a 4-digit PIN:

```javascript
let possiblePasswords = [];
let passwordLength = 4;
let start = 0;
let end = 9;

for (let i = start; i <= end; i++) {
    for (let j = start; j <= end; j++) {
        for (let k = start; k <= end; k++) {
            for (let l = start; l <= end; l++) {
                let password = String(i) + String(j) + String(k) + String(l);
