This script generates all 4-digit numbers from 0000 to 9999 and stores them in the `possiblePasswords` array. You can then use this array to test against your target system.

It's important to note that bruteforcing can be time-consuming and resource-intensive, especially for longer passwords or more complex problems. Also, it's not always ethical or legal to use bruteforcing to gain unauthorized access to systems. Always ensure you have permission to test passwords or other sensitive information.

Lastly, modern systems often have measures in place to prevent bruteforcing, such as locking accounts after a certain number of failed login attempts. Always consider these factors when implementing bruteforcing in your code.

