    public Car(String color) {
        this.color = color;
    }

    public String getColor() {
        return color;
    }
}
```

2. Next, let's create a method to find the most popular car color and its count.

```java
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

public class Main {
    public static Map<String, Integer> getMostPopularCarColor(List<Car> cars) {
        return cars.stream()
                   .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(Car::getColor, Collectors.counting()))
                   .entries()
                   .stream()
                   .max(Map.Entry.comparingByValue())
                   .map(Map.Entry::getKey)
                   .map(color -> Map.of(color, ((Map.Entry<String, Long>)
                                            Map.entry(color,
                                                       ((Map.Entry<String, Long>)
                                                        Map.entry(color,
                                                                   Map.get(color, cars.stream()
                                                                            .filter(car -> car.getColor().equals(color))
                                                                            .count()))))
                                                        .getValue()))
                   .orElse(null);
    }
}
```

3. Finally, use the method to find the most popular car color in a list of cars:

```java
public static void main(String[] args) {
    List<Car> cars = Arrays.asList(
        new Car("Red"),
